GIVEN r IS A `Cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cited identifier is in the index with the printed heading and scope` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision with index key` (r's `cited identifier`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST p THEN
            p's `heading as printed` EQUALS r's `heading of the cited provision as printed`
        AND p's `scope` EQUALS r's `scope of the cited provision`
        AND r's `the pinpoint is present in the text`

